# MacroPal Environment Variables

# ============================================
# Demo Mode Configuration
# ============================================
# Set to "true" to enable demo mode
# Demo mode bypasses authentication and uses local storage
# Perfect for showcasing the app without user accounts
VITE_DEMO_MODE=false

# ============================================
# Firebase Configuration
# ============================================
# Your Firebase project API key
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_firebase_api_key_here

# Google Sign-In Web Client ID
# Required for Google authentication
VITE_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=your_google_web_client_id_here

# ============================================
# AI Features (Optional)
# ============================================
# Optional override for Firebase Functions base URL
# Default in app: https://europe-west1-macropal-zanci19.cloudfunctions.net
# VITE_FUNCTIONS_BASE_URL=https://your-region-your-project.cloudfunctions.net
#
# Google Vision key must be configured as a Firebase Functions secret:
# firebase functions:secrets:set GOOGLE_VISION_API_KEY
# (Do not expose Google Vision keys in frontend env vars.)
# VITE_FUNCTIONS_BASE_URL=

# ============================================
# Food Search — FatSecret (primary) + OpenFoodFacts (fallback)
# ============================================
# Food search is served by the `foodSearch` Cloud Function, which queries the
# FatSecret Platform API (foods.search.v5) via OAuth 1.0 request signing and
# falls back to OpenFoodFacts when FatSecret is unavailable or returns nothing.
#
# The FatSecret consumer credentials are Firebase Functions secrets — they are
# used server-side only and must NEVER be exposed in frontend (VITE_*) env vars:
#   firebase functions:secrets:set FATSECRET_CONSUMER_KEY
#   firebase functions:secrets:set FATSECRET_CONSUMER_SECRET
# Then deploy: firebase deploy --only functions:foodSearch
#
# Notes:
# - OAuth 1.0 is used (not OAuth 2.0) because it needs no token endpoint and no
#   egress-IP allow-list, which suits Cloud Functions' dynamic outbound IPs.
# - A premier_free account is US-localized; generic foods work worldwide, and the
#   OpenFoodFacts fallback covers international brands/barcodes.

# ============================================
# Instructions
# ============================================
# 1. Copy this file to .env in the project root
# 2. Replace placeholder values with your actual keys
# 3. Never commit your .env file to version control
# 4. Rebuild the app after changing environment variables:
#    npm run build
